{"title":"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay C Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_C_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Noemi has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> marbles. Of these, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are blue, and the rest are either red or yellow. If Noemi takes a marble at random without looking, the probability that it is yellow is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f7f4de02215a8c5319886c13b2e291811346e1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. How many of the marbles are red?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_C_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> marbles and the probability of choosing a yellow marble is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/5981d02023f1b50cfdabb1a624c123c135ec0de6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50\\% = \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"69\" height=\"37\" />, there must be a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/f/bff3a3b0be103073aad3b2d2cb7b6ccbb52b2b44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 - \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"80\" height=\"37\" /> probability of choosing a marble that isn't yellow, meaning that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/0/5609800060a29a188dad29c0a729bd7b736c2b04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{N}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"19\" height=\"37\" /> of the marbles are either blue or red.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> marbles are blue, the number of red marbles is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/4/6d4c1d82bd449108180af7b6dbe3c7982d338ec7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{N}{2} - 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"54\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_C_Problem_1\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay C Problem 1\">player 1</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/0/2e09aafff3bcc6cf239ad36a74b4b433df4fb96b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, the number of red marbles is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/3/1f3f99f91ce70a1bf2269cf22662cb06bb80693a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{22}{2} - 5 = 11 - 5 = \\boxed{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"174\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC\">2023 CEMC TUC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=